PE 785: 5-sextuples / 五元组

=== Enumerating 6-tuples from {1,2,3,4,5} ===
=== All 6-tuples from {1,2,3,4,5} ===
Total 6-tuples: 5^6 = 15625

Tuples where sum(first 3) = sum(last 3):
  Count = 1751

Palindromic tuples (a,b,c,c,b,a): 125

Non-decreasing 6-tuples from [1..5]:
  Count = C(10,6) = 210

Tuples with all entries distinct: P(5,6) = 0 (can't have 6 distinct from 5)

=== Sum of squares equality: a²+b² = c²+d²+e²+f² ===
  N=2: count = 6
  N=3: count = 15
  N=4: count = 28
  N=5: count = 45
  N=6: count = 66
  N=7: count = 95
  N=8: count = 132

=== Product equality: a*b*c = d*e*f ===
  N=2: count = 20
  N=3: count = 93
  N=4: count = 340
  N=5: count = 665
  N=6: count = 1746

=== Weighted sums ===
  6-tuples from [1..5] with weighted sum ≡ 0 mod 5: 3125

=== Combinatorial identities ===
  C(n, 6) for various n:
    C( 6,6) = 1
    C( 7,6) = 7
    C( 8,6) = 28
    C( 9,6) = 84
    C(10,6) = 210
    C(11,6) = 462
    C(12,6) = 924
    C(13,6) = 1716
    C(14,6) = 3003
    C(15,6) = 5005
    C(16,6) = 8008
    C(17,6) = 12376
    C(18,6) = 18564
    C(19,6) = 27132
    C(20,6) = 38760
